  "id": "lingual-gyrus",
  "term": "lingual gyrus",
  "definition": "The lingual gyrus is a brain region in the medial occipitotemporal visual area that appears to act as an intermediate stage in visual processing. It is described as linking early encoding of basic visual features with higher-level visual representation involved in recognizing objects.",
